  "description": "The proposal relates to 48 Vicarage Park, SE18 7SU, which is located within the Plumstead Common Conservation Area.\n\nThe works comprise the alteration of the existing front boundary wall and the erection of a small steel platform within the front lightwell area adjacent to the entrance walkway.\n\nThe existing front boundary wall, currently approximately 0.65 metres in height, will be increased in height to align with the proposed steel platform (approximately 0.8 metres). No metal railings are proposed to the front boundary wall.\n\nThe proposed steel platform will measure approximately 2.3 metres in length and 0.8 metres in height. It will be positioned beside the existing front walkway to enlarge the usable frontage and provide space for bin storage. The platform will be constructed from 50x50x5mm steel SHS members with galvanised expanded mesh infill panels, fixed in accordance with the submitted drawings.\n\nA metal balustrade measuring approximately 1 metre in height and 2.02 metres in width will be installed along the side of the platform, between the house and the existing front boundary wall, to provide a safety barrier adjacent to the lightwell area.\n\nThe works are minor in scale and confined to the front boundary/lightwell area only. No alterations are proposed to the main dwelling, roof, or rear elevation. The proposal is designed to preserve the character and appearance of the Plumstead Common Conservation Area.\n\nWork has begin, but we've not made any of the changes that we're seeking planning permission for. The changes so far are like-for-like repair work.",
